  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(116.06pt, 158.18pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(119.3pt, 161.66pt, "Institute of Energy Research and Development (IERD), BCSIR, Dhaka-1205, Bangladesh  ")
  #line-at(238.37pt, 187.22pt, "*Email: smina@phy.ku.ac.bd ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 214.82pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.624pt, 241.46pt, "NiO/ZnO-based thin films, including single-layer and heterostructure configurations, were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 254.18pt, "synthesized to investigate the influence of stacking order on their electrochemical performance for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 266.81pt, "supercapacitor applications. To improve the relatively low capacitive performance of ZnO compared to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 279.41pt, "NiO, NaCl was introduced as a dopant. All films were deposited using a non-vacuum spin-coating ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 292.13pt, "method on fluorine-doped tin oxide (FTO) substrates, chosen for their excellent electrical conductivity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 304.73pt, "and stability as electrode materials. The surface morphology and structural parameters were examined ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 317.45pt, "using scanning electron microscopy (SEM) and X-ray diffraction (XRD), respectively. Optical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 330.05pt, "properties were analyzed via UV–Vis spectroscopy, revealing direct band gaps in the range of 3.17–")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 342.65pt, "3.31 eV for ZnO and Na–ZnO, and wider gaps up to 3.81 eV for NiO. Electrochemical performance ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 355.37pt, "was evaluated using cyclic voltammetry (CV), galvanostatic charge–discharge (GCD), and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 367.97pt, "electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) in a three-electrode configuration with 1 M KOH as the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.69pt, "electrolyte. Among the electrodes, the single-layer NiO film exhibited the highest specific capacitance ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.29pt, "of 1.391 F g⁻¹. In contrast, the NiO/ZnO heterostructure demonstrated a synergistic effect, resulting in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 405.89pt, "enhanced charge storage and achieving a maximum specific capacitance of 1.627 F g⁻¹ at a current ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 418.61pt, "density of 2.0 mA cm⁻². Furthermore, sodium doping significantly improved the capacitance of ZnO. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 431.21pt, "Overall, the results highlight the potential of sol–gel-derived oxide heterostructures and doped thin films ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 443.95pt, "as cost-effective and scalable electrode materials for supercapacitors in portable electronics and energy ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 456.55pt, "storage systems. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 484.39pt, "1")
  #line-at(93.624pt, 484.39pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.624pt, 510.19pt, "Effective energy harvesting and storage are essential to maintaining the stability of modern power ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 523.87pt, "networks, especially with the increasing dependence on renewable sources that are inherently ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 537.55pt, "intermittent and unevenly distributed. A wide range of energy technologies, encompassing solar, wind, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 551.11pt, "hydroelectric, tidal, and nuclear power")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(242.81pt, 547.15pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(246.29pt, 551.11pt, ", have been developed and show great potential for sustainable ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 564.79pt, "power generation. Despite their advantages, renewable energy sources face challenges such as ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 578.47pt, "intermittency, location constraints, and a mismatch between energy generation and consumption ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 592.15pt, "demands. Hence, global energy demand still depends predominantly on fossil fuels. The continued ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 605.71pt, "combustion of these non-renewable resources emits substantial quantities of carbon dioxide and other ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 619.42pt, "greenhouse gases, exacerbating environmental damage and climate change. environmental degradation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 633.1pt, "and accelerating climate-related challenges. As a result, there is a rising desire to find new energy ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 646.78pt, "sources that can be used instead of fossil fuels.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 674.02pt, "Conventional batteries are commonly used to balance fluctuations between energy generation and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 687.7pt, "consumption. Despite their widespread use, batteries suffer from limited power density, which hampers ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 701.38pt, "their performance in high-power applications. Supercapacitors, by comparison, have emerged as an ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 714.94pt, "attractive energy storage technology, characterized by high power density and rapid charge–discharge ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 728.62pt, "behavior")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(110.66pt, 724.66pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.14pt, 728.62pt, ". These devices are commonly divided into three categories according to their energy storage ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 742.296pt, "mechanisms and structural properties: electric double-layer capacitors (EDLCs), pseudocapacitors, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 755.976pt, "hybrid supercapacitors. A supercapacitor operates by placing two parallel conductive electrodes ")
]

