#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.46pt, 789.576pt, "Page ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.58pt, 789.576pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.22pt, 789.576pt, " of ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(512.26pt, 789.576pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.08pt, "separated by a dielectric medium. When a voltage is applied to one electrode and the other is grounded, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 95.78pt, "opposite charges accumulate on each surface until electrostatic equilibrium is established. Therefore, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 109.46pt, "the efficiency and overall performance of a supercapacitor is strongly influenced by the fabrication ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 122.9pt, "process and the properties of the electrode materials.")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.62pt, "Transition metal oxides (TMOs) like nickel oxide (NiO), zinc oxide (ZnO), manganese dioxide ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 157.22pt, "(MnO2), and cobalt oxide (Co3O4) have become potential pseudocapacitive materials because of their ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 169.82pt, "multivalency and high theoretical capacitance ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(282.17pt, 165.86pt, "3,4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(290.93pt, 169.82pt, ". Of these, NiO and ZnO are particularly appealing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 182.54pt, "owing to their abundance, lack of toxicity, and electronically tailorable properties. NiO, a p-type ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 195.14pt, "semiconductor, possesses high specific capacitance (up to 1292 F g-1) and excellent electrochemical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.86pt, "stability ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(110.3pt, 203.9pt, "5,6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(119.06pt, 207.86pt, ". ZnO, traditionally used in sensors and photovoltaics, has more recently shown promise for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 220.46pt, "application in supercapacitors, especially when doped or combined with other oxides ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(449.26pt, 216.5pt, "7,8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(458.02pt, 220.46pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 245.78pt, "Compared to powder-based electrodes, thin-film electrodes fabricated on conductive substrates like ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 258.38pt, "fluorine-doped tin oxide (FTO) glass exhibit distinct advantages. These include better interfacial ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 271.13pt, "contact, thickness control, and compatibility for integration in microsystems ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(414.43pt, 267.17pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.91pt, 271.13pt, ". Thin films also enable ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 283.73pt, "detailed studies of the charge transport mechanism and optimizing electrochemical properties through ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 296.45pt, "morphology, composition, or heterostructure design changes. The deliberate incorporation of ZnO and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 309.05pt, "NiO into heterojunction architectures (i.e., ZnO/NiO or NiO/ZnO) has manifested synergistic effects to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 321.65pt, "promote charge separation, ion diffusion, and redox activity, and hence improved capacitive ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 334.37pt, "performance ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.66pt, 330.41pt, "4,8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(140.42pt, 334.37pt, ". This forms the core motivation behind our study, which investigates the capacitive ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 346.97pt, "characteristics of undoped and sodium-doped ZnO, NiO, and their heterostructures fabricated on FTO ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 359.69pt, "substrates. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 384.89pt, "In this study, ZnO, Na-doped ZnO (Na–ZnO), and NiO thin films, along with their heterostructures, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 397.61pt, "were synthesized and systematically investigated as electrode materials for supercapacitor applications. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 410.21pt, "The motivation stems from the complementary properties of ZnO and NiO—ZnO offering excellent ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.93pt, "chemical stability and wide band gap transparency, while NiO provides rich redox activity and high ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 435.53pt, "theoretical capacitance. Sodium doping was introduced into ZnO to enhance electrical conductivity and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 448.15pt, "defect-mediated ion transport, addressing its intrinsic limitations as a pure oxide. By engineering ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 460.87pt, "ZnO/NiO and NiO/Na–ZnO heterostructures, this work aims to exploit interfacial coupling and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 473.47pt, "synergistic charge transfer between the constituent oxides to improve electrochemical performance. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 486.19pt, "Comprehensive optical and electrochemical characterizations reveal how doping, thickness, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 498.79pt, "stacking order influence band structure, redox kinetics, and charge storage behavior, providing valuable ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 511.51pt, "insight into the rational design of next-generation oxide-based supercapacitor electrodes. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 537.31pt, "2")
  #line-at(93.624pt, 537.31pt, "Experimental Procedures ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 553.99pt, "2.1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 553.99pt, "Precursor and Chemical Additives")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 579.67pt, "Analytical-grade zinc acetate dihydrate (Zn(CH₃COO)₂·2H₂O), nickel nitrate hexahydrate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 593.35pt, "(Ni(NO₃)₂·6H₂O), mono-ethanolamine (MEA), sodium chloride (NaCl), and 2-methoxy ethanol were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 607.03pt, "used with no additional filtration. Fluorine-doped tin oxide (FTO) glass substrates (sheet resistance: ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 620.5pt, "10–15 Ω sq⁻¹) served as deposition bases. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 643.3pt, "2.2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 643.3pt, "Deposition of NiO/ZnO Composite and Single Layers on FTO Substrate ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 670.78pt, "The spin-coating method was used to deposit all of the films. Fluorine-doped tin oxide (FTO) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 683.38pt, "coated glass substrates were chosen for their high optical transparency, good chemical stability, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 696.1pt, "low sheet resistance (10 – 20 Ω sq⁻¹), providing an excellent conducting platform for film deposition ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 708.7pt, "and subsequent electrochemical measurements. The thicknesses of single-layer ZnO and NiO films ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 721.42pt, "were approximately 125 nm and 75 nm, respectively. As these individual layers were relatively thin, all ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 734.02pt, "films were deposited with ten consecutive spin-coated layers to achieve an optimal overall thickness ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 746.736pt, "suitable for reliable performance analysis. ")
]

