#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 451.5pt), 72pt, 196pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.46pt, 789.576pt, "Page ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.58pt, 789.576pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.22pt, 789.576pt, " of ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(512.26pt, 789.576pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 81.96pt, "The substrates were first cleaned manually with methanol and acetone, rinsed with distilled water, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 94.58pt, "ultrasonicated sequentially in methanol, acetone, and distilled water for 10 min each. Finally, an oxygen ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 107.3pt, "plasma treatment was applied for 1 min at 80 W to enhance surface adhesion. The ZnO sol (0.4 M) was ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 119.9pt, "prepared by dissolving zinc acetate dihydrate in ethanol with three drops of monoethanolamine (MEA) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 132.62pt, "as a stabilizer. The solution was stirred at 70 °C for 1 h and aged for 24 h. Similarly, a 0.3 M NiO sol ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 145.22pt, "was obtained by dissolving nickel nitrate hexahydrate in ethanol under identical conditions. Sodium-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 157.82pt, "doped ZnO (Na–ZnO) sol was prepared by adding 0.5 wt% NaCl to 10 ml of ZnO sol, followed by the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 170.54pt, "same stirring and aging steps. All precursor solutions were filtered prior to coating to remove any ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 183.14pt, "undissolved impurities.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 445.03pt, "A two-stage spin-coating technique was employed for thin-film deposition, with rotational speeds of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 457.75pt, "2500 rpm for 10 s and 3200 rpm for 22 s. Each layer was dried at 300 °C for 10 min, and the deposition–")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.35pt, "drying cycle was reenacted ten times to obtain the required film thickness. The final films were annealed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 483.07pt, "at 500°C for 1 h in air with a heating rate of 5°C min⁻¹. For NiO films, the heating rate was reduced to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 495.67pt, "2°C min⁻¹ to prevent cracking. During deposition, part of each substrate was masked with Kapton tape ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 508.27pt, "to maintain a clean contact region for later electrical characterization. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 533.59pt, "Single-layer (NiO, ZnO, Na–ZnO) and bilayer heterostructures (NiO/ZnO, ZnO/NiO, Na–ZnO/NiO, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 546.31pt, "NiO/Na–ZnO) were fabricated sequentially. The first layer was deposited and annealed before applying ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 558.91pt, "the second. These stacking configurations were designed to study the impact of layer order and sodium ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 571.51pt, "doping on electrochemical performance. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 597.31pt, "2.3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 597.31pt, "Material Characterization ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 622.9pt, "Material formation and elemental analysis at the nanoscale of the prepared films were inspected ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 636.58pt, "using a field-emission scanning electron microscope (SEM, EVO 18, EDAX, AMETEK, USA). The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 650.26pt, "crystal structure and phase formation were analyzed by X-ray diffraction (XRD) using a GBC Matrix ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 663.94pt, "SSD diffractometer with Cu Kα radiation. Optical absorption spectra were recorded with a UV–Vis ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 677.5pt, "spectrophotometer (UH4150, Hitachi, Japan) to determine the optical properties and estimate the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 691.18pt, "bandgap energy of the films. Electrochemical measurements were performed using a CHI660E ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 704.86pt, "electrochemical workstation. The film thicknesses were measured using a Bruker DektakXT stylus ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 718.42pt, "profilometer to ensure uniformity and consistency across all samples. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 390.41pt, "Figure 1:")
  #line-at(114.86pt, 390.41pt, "Schematic representation of the fabricated NiO/ZnO heterostructure, illustrating the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 403.01pt, "NiO/ZnO stacking sequence and the formation of a supercapacitor when employed as the working ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 415.85pt, "electrode in a three-electrode electrochemical setup.")
]

