  #line-at(100.82pt, 83.04pt, "Electrochemical Measurements ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 108.74pt, "A conventional three-electrode configuration was employed for all electrochemical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 122.3pt, "measurements. Films deposited on the FTO substrate were used as the working electrode, which was ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 135.98pt, "submerged in a 1 M KOH aqueous electrolyte with an exposed active area of approximately 0.2827 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 149.66pt, "cm². A platinum wire acted as the counter electrode, and an Ag/AgCl electrode was used as the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 163.34pt, "reference. Cyclic voltammetry (CV) was performed at scan rates ranging from 5 to 100 mV s⁻¹, while ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 176.9pt, "galvanostatic charge–discharge (GCD) measurements were conducted at current densities between 0.2 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 190.58pt, "and 2.0 mA cm⁻², depending on the electrode composition. The voltage window was (0-0.6)V. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 217.34pt, "3")
  #line-at(93.624pt, 217.34pt, "Result and Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 244.1pt, "3.1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.82pt, 244.1pt, "Structural Characterization and Surface Morphology  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.02pt, 269.69pt, "The XRD pattern of ZnO (Figure 12) displays prominent peaks at 31.76°, 34.42°, and 36.26°, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 283.37pt, "which correspond to the (100), (002), and (101) planes of hexagonal wurtzite ZnO (JCPDS card no. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 297.05pt, "36-1451). The dominant (002) peak indicates a strong c-axis orientation, commonly observed in ZnO ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 310.73pt, "films derived from sol–gel spin coating ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(248.09pt, 306.77pt, "10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.05pt, 310.73pt, ". This preferred orientation is known to enhance electron ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 324.29pt, "mobility and surface energy uniformity, which are desirable for optoelectronic and capacitive ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 337.97pt, "applications. No additional peaks were detected, confirming phase purity and effective crystallization ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 352.49pt, "under the employed annealing conditions ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(256.37pt, 347.93pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
