  #line-at(520.78pt, 107.3pt, ", ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 119.9pt, "thereby enhancing overall capacitance. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 145.22pt, "The GCD profiles exhibited nonlinear, quasi-triangular shapes typical of pseudocapacitive materials")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.82pt, 141.26pt, "29")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(520.78pt, 145.22pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 157.82pt, "NiO electrodes showed the longest discharge times, while Na–ZnO displayed improved discharge ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 170.54pt, "duration compared to undoped ZnO, confirming the beneficial role of Na in facilitating charge transfer. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 183.14pt, "Among all EDLC samples, NiO/Na–ZnO showed the longest discharge time and most symmetric ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 195.86pt, "charge–discharge profile, reflecting efficient and reversible energy storage. This indicates that Na ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 208.46pt, "doping and heterostructure formation synergistically enhance electrochemical activity by improving ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 221.06pt, "conductivity, redox kinetics, and ion accessibility.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 246.38pt, "The overall capacitance values (1–2 F g⁻¹) were lower than optimized systems reported in literature [14] ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 259.1pt, "[16], this limitation can be attributed to the restricted exposure of the electrode’s active surface to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 271.73pt, "electrolyte. This is why the CV and GCD could not be performed for various scan rates. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 299.57pt, "Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 321.29pt, "This work explored the design of NiO/ZnO thin films, both as single layers and heterostructures, with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 333.89pt, "sodium doping introduced to overcome the inherent limitations of ZnO. The objective was to explore ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 346.61pt, "the capacitive performance of pure NiO and ZnO TCMs. Followed by how the composite NiO/ZnO ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 359.21pt, "behaves differently. By combining structural, optical, and electrochemical analyses, we showed that the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 371.93pt, "order of stacking and the presence of dopants play a decisive role in the charge storage behavior of these ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 384.53pt, "films. The NiO/ZnO heterostructure, in particular, revealed a clear synergistic effect, achieving a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 397.13pt, "specific capacitance higher than either oxide alone. ZnO's performance was further improved by sodium ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 409.85pt, "doping, demonstrating how small chemical changes can reveal new possibilities in otherwise ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.45pt, "unremarkable materials. Even though the obtained capacitance value was low, these results suggest a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 435.17pt, "more general message: transparent oxide heterostructures derived from sol-gel are not only scalable and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 447.79pt, "affordable, but they also provide a flexible platform for customising electrochemical properties. Their ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 460.39pt, "potential is in connecting basic material science with real-world energy storage requirements, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 473.11pt, "particularly in portable electronics where cost and efficiency are crucial. In the future, developing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 485.71pt, "dopant strategies, investigating different oxide pairings, and evaluating long-term cycling stability will ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 498.43pt, "be crucial steps in converting these laboratory discoveries into practical supercapacitor technologies. ")
